{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, upon the Gittith</b> — This psalm was given to the families of Obed-Edom the Gittite, who is from the sons of Levi, like Jeduthun; or it is a poem whose beginning is 'the Gittith,' from a term of glory and the like. And Rabbi Moses said: for it is an instrument attributed to the family of Obed-Edom the Gittite. But such an attribution we have not found. And the inebriated said: upon a tune of those who tread the winepress."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:36.822223681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}